That's always the thing, indoctrinate our children, even though most of the people talking about this do not have students at Texas A&M and they're grown ass adults, most of which did not go to college.

53:08.904 --> 53:10.345
You do not have any skin in this game.

53:11.245 --> 53:12.326
You have none whatsoever.

53:14.486 --> 53:16.327
The average American does not read more than one book a year.

53:19.372 --> 53:20.213
So who are y'all mad at?

53:20.734 --> 53:21.716
Who are y'all mad at?

53:22.217 --> 53:25.683
So... Yeah.

53:26.905 --> 53:28.086
So, like, the frustration is...

53:30.890 --> 53:37.131
Yes, yes, I'd say I think Mark Welsh was kind of that turning the new page, turning a new leaf.

53:37.171 --> 53:40.572
I think he was making wonderful changes, like making tick a poll online.

53:41.152 --> 53:48.533
He was talking about decreasing admissions the next five years to kind of combat the congestion that we feel in College Station and Bryan.

53:48.933 --> 53:52.474
I think these were lovely, real conversations to be having.

53:52.854 --> 53:56.834
And my question is, he's a retired something Starry General.

53:57.615 --> 53:59.355
If he's not Texas A&M material,

54:00.215 --> 54:00.555
Who is?

54:01.856 --> 54:02.476
Who do you want?

54:02.976 --> 54:07.477
Because picture perfect.

54:07.658 --> 54:09.538
It's picture perfect.

54:12.019 --> 54:12.219
So.

54:14.260 --> 54:17.781
Because remember, he left because Republican lawmakers were giving him shit on Twitter.

54:19.365 --> 54:23.929
saying you didn't do something fast enough when he stand by his professors and educators.

54:24.569 --> 54:29.053
Because he acknowledged, hey, I don't have a degree in English lit.

54:29.713 --> 54:32.516
I'm going to let her decide what's appropriate.

54:32.536 --> 54:41.623
And that's 100% what the average boss does is acknowledging when it's not my profession.

54:41.683 --> 54:43.505
It's just not what I know the most about.

54:44.986 --> 54:48.669
It's a level of humility that I admired so deeply in him.

54:49.214 --> 54:50.314
And to see that get punished.

54:50.334 --> 54:51.855
That is sad.

54:51.875 --> 54:52.055
Yes.

54:53.195 --> 54:53.815
Heartbreaking.

54:53.835 --> 54:54.236
Heartbreaking.

54:54.276 --> 54:55.396
No, and it's been boiling.

54:56.396 --> 55:06.639
And, you know, I kept checking every day on Howdy during winter break to see if my sex and gender class was being canceled, edited, removed, what have you.

55:06.960 --> 55:07.900
And I just kept checking it.

55:08.020 --> 55:11.101
And, okay, I'll show up for a second class.

55:11.341 --> 55:12.781
Okay, I'm going to show up second week class.

55:14.502 --> 55:14.862
We'll see.

55:15.202 --> 55:17.963
How are you living with those emotions now?

55:19.400 --> 55:21.341
I've been carrying it mainly internally.

55:21.361 --> 55:23.903
I have not posted anything on social media.

55:24.583 --> 55:27.165
Cause again, then I'm a target and the history department's a target.

55:27.205 --> 55:28.646
I'm an employee of Texas A&M.

55:28.666 --> 55:29.746
I'm not protected by tenure.

55:30.067 --> 55:31.247
And it's been proven that doesn't help you.

55:33.389 --> 55:34.369
There's nothing protecting me.

55:35.390 --> 55:36.551
And that is incredibly scary.

55:38.892 --> 55:46.157
And again, I'm not the angry bra burning feminist that they think is taking these classes.

55:47.669 --> 55:52.952
I'm taking these classes because indigenous peoples have different ideas of what being a woman and being a man is.

55:54.792 --> 55:55.373
Simple as that.

55:58.114 --> 55:58.734
Even if you were.

55:59.054 --> 56:01.035
And even if I was, who cares?

56:01.075 --> 56:01.956
I'm giving A&M money.

56:02.696 --> 56:03.336
Even if you were.

56:03.917 --> 56:04.997
Even if I were.

56:06.018 --> 56:06.898
What's it to you?

56:07.438 --> 56:08.299
Who is it to you?

56:08.699 --> 56:10.640
Who is the government to say what I can and can't read?

56:10.740 --> 56:11.180
I'm yelling.

56:11.220 --> 56:11.640
I'm sorry.

56:11.900 --> 56:12.761
That's fine.

56:13.474 --> 56:21.298
Yeah, it's incredibly frustrating because it's such a slippery slope of who are you to say what can and can't be taught, what I can and can't read.

56:21.518 --> 56:26.400
There's a definition of government overreach from the so-and-so small government party.

56:26.680 --> 56:27.721
That's what's infuriating.

56:30.902 --> 56:32.783
Yeah.

56:32.803 --> 56:33.124
Yeah.

56:33.264 --> 56:34.264
Yeah.

56:35.305 --> 56:35.485
Yeah.

56:35.565 --> 56:40.247
And to make this decision as an interim president, shame on you.

56:41.508 --> 56:42.208
Shame on you.

56:45.230 --> 56:45.430
Yeah.

56:46.671 --> 56:52.433
I don't think people realize, or maybe they do, and they just don't care, that there's people behind these choices.

56:52.493 --> 56:54.814
Not just the choices, but the effect.

56:55.675 --> 56:56.775
That people are out of a job.

56:57.675 --> 56:58.636
They can't feed their family.

56:58.736 --> 57:00.016
Americans are out of jobs.

57:00.076 --> 57:01.117
Americans are out of jobs.

57:01.137 --> 57:02.437
They can't feed their family.

57:03.038 --> 57:06.139
Especially in this market, this job market.

57:07.720 --> 57:12.402
And not only that, is the students that would take these classes,

57:13.604 --> 57:14.164
That signed up.

57:14.184 --> 57:15.065
They were curious.

57:15.645 --> 57:16.726
They wanted to learn something.

57:17.246 --> 57:19.248
They said they were told, no, you can't.

57:19.348 --> 57:20.068
You can't do that.

57:20.088 --> 57:20.989
You can't be curious.

57:21.009 --> 57:27.013
I know I'm supposed to be asking questions.

57:27.313 --> 57:28.374
No, but I'm glad.

57:28.554 --> 57:31.256
No, it's just, it's infuriating.

57:31.656 --> 57:32.797
But I do have hope.

57:33.697 --> 57:38.640
I see on Facebook comments, so many people are angry about this.

57:38.660 --> 57:39.401
Mm-hmm.

57:40.925 --> 57:44.188
So many people are angry about this, and that makes me so happy.

57:46.450 --> 57:49.112
That it's not just people on campus.

57:49.592 --> 57:52.895
After I just said, you know, if you don't have skin in this game, who cares?

57:53.696 --> 57:55.297
And I completely acknowledge that's hypocritical.

57:55.917 --> 57:59.781
But people are mad.

58:00.481 --> 58:01.862
People are saying this is not my A&M.

58:02.723 --> 58:03.964
I'm embarrassed to be an Aggie.

58:04.024 --> 58:07.347
It's the same conversations OU was having a couple months ago.

58:09.781 --> 58:13.163
Because it's antithetical to the idea of an Aggie.

58:13.303 --> 58:13.463
Yes.

58:15.043 --> 58:15.764
You're not respecting.

58:16.144 --> 58:16.584
Not respecting.

58:16.884 --> 58:17.404
No integrity.

58:18.865 --> 58:19.005
No.

58:21.987 --> 58:23.207
What is that?

58:24.668 --> 58:29.310
We might have differences, but you come together, discuss it respectfully.

58:30.871 --> 58:36.193
I think that is what an Aggie is literally bred to do when you're here.

58:37.543 --> 58:47.333
That was one of the first things I learned was when I was reading history, that you might have differences, but you respect each other and talk about it.

58:47.854 --> 58:52.879
Yeah, because that happens even in, I'm sure, so many ag classrooms.

58:53.600 --> 58:55.482
Well, I think we should breed this heifer on this day.

58:55.962 --> 58:57.384
Well, I think we should do it this day.

58:57.404 --> 58:57.764
Mm-hmm.

58:58.485 --> 59:01.346
That's a completely different, we're not talking about literature.

59:01.747 --> 59:09.630
We're talking about something concrete, real that we can touch and feel, but we're still having a disagreement and we have to have a civil conversation about how to remedy that.

59:10.190 --> 59:11.311
And that's what you're taking away.

59:12.512 --> 59:13.072
Very much so.

59:13.092 --> 59:13.272
Yeah.

59:15.853 --> 59:24.057
How does this, I think I know the answer, but how does this make you feel about the future of this university?

59:27.942 --> 59:32.285
It depends on if Abbott's re-elected, if I can be completely honest with you.

59:32.565 --> 59:40.130
It entirely hinges upon Abbott being re-elected because with his new foreign visa ban he wants to implement, that's going to impact us.

59:40.150 --> 59:41.030
That's going to impact UT.

59:41.090 --> 59:43.131
It's going to impact thousands of students.

59:44.172 --> 59:54.098
It is an honor that someone in Taiwan wants to leave their family and come here when it's 80 degrees on Christmas and humidity is 100%.

59:54.118 --> 59:54.659
That's an honor for

59:58.738 --> 59:59.898
And the American dream.

59:59.998 --> 01:00:01.159
That is the American dream.

01:00:01.859 --> 01:00:05.000
And you are robbing that of thousands, thousands of people.

01:00:06.361 --> 01:00:06.901
And their families.

01:00:07.621 --> 01:00:08.321
And their families.

01:00:08.401 --> 01:00:16.184
And it breaks my heart to know that we might lose an R1 distinction, which is the pinnacle of academic success.

01:00:16.904 --> 01:00:19.765
We spend, I think, close to a billion dollars in research a year.

01:00:19.785 --> 01:00:22.306
More than that.

01:00:22.326 --> 01:00:22.626
More than that.

01:00:23.746 --> 01:00:24.847
It's put food on my table.

01:00:24.867 --> 01:00:25.287
Mm-hmm.

01:00:26.593 --> 01:00:27.633
Keeps my lights on.

01:00:28.654 --> 01:00:31.535
You're impacting thousands of Americans with these decisions.

01:00:32.095 --> 01:00:32.916
And soon to be Americans.

01:00:33.396 --> 01:00:33.676
Yes.

01:00:34.216 --> 01:00:34.436
So.

01:00:34.456 --> 01:00:36.837
It's turning away people who want to be American.

01:00:37.338 --> 01:00:37.478
Yep.

01:00:37.678 --> 01:00:38.478
Want to be Texans.

01:00:38.938 --> 01:00:39.419
Want to be Texans.

01:00:39.459 --> 01:00:39.819
Want to be Aggies.

01:00:39.979 --> 01:00:40.159
Yes.

01:00:40.739 --> 01:00:41.499
Absolutely.

01:00:41.519 --> 01:00:41.740
100%.

01:00:42.620 --> 01:00:44.141
So that's what I'm more worried about.

01:00:44.381 --> 01:00:47.922
The second we lose that R1, we lose professors, we lose grad students.

01:00:48.162 --> 01:00:48.382
Sure.

01:00:49.083 --> 01:00:54.005
I've been jokingly encouraged to think about other places.

01:00:54.025 --> 01:00:54.245
Sure.

01:00:59.438 --> 01:01:01.839
I think it's heartbreaking.

01:01:03.419 --> 01:01:04.200
And something needs to change.

01:01:04.800 --> 01:01:06.120
At a state level.

01:01:06.220 --> 01:01:12.302
Till I go blue in the face, this is not a university level.

01:01:12.563 --> 01:01:14.223
This is a state level decision.

01:01:18.105 --> 01:01:19.605
There's been six flags over Texas.

01:01:21.266 --> 01:01:22.946
So we are not a homogenous people.

01:01:23.506 --> 01:01:25.027
I don't know where y'all got that idea from.

01:01:27.194 --> 01:01:34.659
You go through an H-E-B, how many lines of other countries are you seeing that you can shop from?

01:01:34.679 --> 01:01:39.581
Yep.

01:01:39.621 --> 01:01:39.862
So.

01:01:42.143 --> 01:01:43.404
Oh, that's very valid.

01:01:43.424 --> 01:01:43.904
Yep, yep, yep, yep.

01:01:45.105 --> 01:01:46.706
Thank you for sharing those things.

01:01:46.726 --> 01:01:47.426
Yeah, of course.

01:01:47.947 --> 01:01:48.247
Yeah.

01:01:49.868 --> 01:01:51.989
How's the general...

01:01:54.187 --> 01:01:57.509
We're terrified.

01:01:58.930 --> 01:01:59.791
We're hopeful though.

01:02:00.091 --> 01:02:03.393
It is such, it is the best of times and the worst of times, really and truly.

01:02:03.413 --> 01:02:04.394
We are so excited.

01:02:04.694 --> 01:02:06.195
We're hiring three new faculty this year.

01:02:06.716 --> 01:02:09.918
So obviously there's still, there's still interest.

01:02:10.358 --> 01:02:13.480
There's still attractiveness to be at A&M and we don't take that for granted.

01:02:13.500 --> 01:02:17.283
We just sent out our acceptance letters for the new cohort for grad students.

01:02:17.583 --> 01:02:18.564
That's so exciting.

01:02:20.357 --> 01:02:25.741
So it is this very bittersweet time where we keep looking over our shoulders.

01:02:28.343 --> 01:02:34.969
What would help this department and also just the faculty and staff in general?

01:02:35.969 --> 01:02:42.775
Trust, feeling like we are trusted to do our jobs that we were hired to do, that we were accepted to do.

01:02:46.277 --> 01:02:48.699
Go away with the syllabus review.

01:02:48.719 --> 01:02:53.082
I completely understand wanting to update course descriptions.

01:02:53.102 --> 01:02:54.463
Some of those are 50 years old.

01:02:56.705 --> 01:03:01.088
But you're hiring someone who's an expert in a field you might know nothing about.

01:03:02.029 --> 01:03:06.753
I would trust them any day to say what's appropriate or not to teach.

01:03:07.514 --> 01:03:09.735
Very fair.

01:03:11.016 --> 01:03:12.297
Yeah.

01:03:12.377 --> 01:03:12.878
I would say that.

01:03:14.384 --> 01:03:19.185
Or heavy, literal statement saying that we're not touching anything else.

01:03:20.585 --> 01:03:20.965
We're good.

01:03:21.825 --> 01:03:24.046
And this should have been done before the semester started.

01:03:24.066 --> 01:03:27.086
Yeah, very much.

01:03:27.347 --> 01:03:28.127
Was it two weeks?

01:03:28.207 --> 01:03:29.127
They gave people two weeks?

01:03:29.227 --> 01:03:29.427
Yeah.

01:03:29.507 --> 01:03:30.487
That's not enough time.

01:03:30.527 --> 01:03:31.487
No, right before Christmas?

01:03:31.507 --> 01:03:32.247
Not enough time.

01:03:32.267 --> 01:03:33.048
Are you kidding?

01:03:33.228 --> 01:03:34.948
People don't check their email.

01:03:34.968 --> 01:03:35.028
No.

01:03:35.308 --> 01:03:37.969
Sorry, that's... No, no, like, no.

01:03:38.549 --> 01:03:39.869
No, it's complete, no.

01:03:41.627 --> 01:03:42.908
Again, you have to ask this question.

01:03:42.928 --> 01:03:44.209
Are we a business or are we a school?

01:03:45.470 --> 01:03:46.510
We're being treated like the former.

01:03:47.871 --> 01:03:50.253
So, just lay off.

01:03:50.293 --> 01:03:51.894
I think that's the thing.

01:03:51.934 --> 01:03:52.554
Lay off.

01:03:52.734 --> 01:03:53.955
Let me do what I need to do.

01:03:54.335 --> 01:03:56.276
Yeah, let the school be school.

01:03:56.937 --> 01:03:57.117
Yeah.

01:03:58.738 --> 01:04:01.220
Yeah.

01:04:01.260 --> 01:04:10.165
The people who say, what would you say to people who are, that have that fear of, they actually legitimately have that fear of you're going to indoctrinate my kids.

01:04:10.205 --> 01:04:11.446
What would you say to them?

01:04:12.046 --> 01:04:13.607
They've been living at your house for 20 years.

01:04:14.368 --> 01:04:18.651
You have to trust that the morals you raised them with are gonna withstand.

01:04:20.072 --> 01:04:27.978
And I think it is wonderful that they're being questioned, and they might come out the other end stronger in the beliefs that you taught them.

01:04:28.158 --> 01:04:31.280
110%, that is a real possibility.

01:04:33.922 --> 01:04:34.122
Yeah.

01:04:35.163 --> 01:04:40.327
If you're nervous about a 16-week course completely transforming your child into an unrecognizable person,

01:04:41.250 --> 01:04:42.971
I think you need to have lunch with your kid.

01:04:44.112 --> 01:04:46.434
Are you talking to your student weekly?

01:04:46.654 --> 01:04:47.555
Are you checking in on them?

01:04:47.575 --> 01:04:48.896
Are you just sending them Venmos?

01:04:49.697 --> 01:04:49.877
Yeah.

01:04:51.759 --> 01:04:54.040
Are you having a real relationship with your child?

01:04:54.681 --> 01:04:55.722
What's more important to you?

01:04:57.043 --> 01:05:00.305
My dad said he'd rather I come home pregnant than a liberal when I went to college.

01:05:00.326 --> 01:05:03.108
That's rough.

01:05:03.128 --> 01:05:03.228
Yes.

01:05:03.248 --> 01:05:07.812
That's actually been upsetting.

01:05:07.832 --> 01:05:07.992
Yes.

01:05:08.012 --> 01:05:08.092
Yes.

01:05:11.840 --> 01:05:12.740
What's more important to you?

01:05:12.760 --> 01:05:15.161
How your child votes?

01:05:15.901 --> 01:05:17.801
Or how they love and respect and treat others?

01:05:21.942 --> 01:05:22.342
I get it.

01:05:22.402 --> 01:05:24.582
I get the idea of sending your kid off.

01:05:24.602 --> 01:05:29.643
I find it funny that people from other states come here because I'm like, how did you hear about us?

01:05:31.183 --> 01:05:31.864
I completely get it.

01:05:31.944 --> 01:05:36.044
You're sending your kid thousands of miles away, hours away.

01:05:36.064 --> 01:05:38.865
Hell, if you're in El Paso, you're not seeing your kid until Christmas.

01:05:40.011 --> 01:05:41.712
So I completely get that.

01:05:41.772 --> 01:05:47.853
It's just up to you to still engage because raising a child is not done once they hit 18.

01:05:48.854 --> 01:05:53.775
That relationship doesn't dissolve just because they're in class.

01:05:53.795 --> 01:05:56.056
So ask yourself, what's more important?

01:05:56.696 --> 01:05:57.916
Maintain that relationship.

01:05:58.936 --> 01:06:02.117
Have room in your mind and heart to be challenged yourself.

01:06:03.258 --> 01:06:04.458
We're not saying you're wrong.

01:06:04.478 --> 01:06:05.398
You're a horrible person.

01:06:05.438 --> 01:06:06.419
You're going to burn in hell.

01:06:06.459 --> 01:06:07.539
No one's saying that.

01:06:09.493 --> 01:06:12.921
Difficult conversations are wonderful to have and you will come out stronger together.

01:06:13.302 --> 01:06:14.244
I promise you.

01:06:14.264 --> 01:06:16.950
Thank you.

01:06:24.855 --> 01:06:32.519
I think parents right now are just, there's anxieties in the country as a whole, and they're just, what is the closest thing that resembles that right now?

01:06:32.599 --> 01:06:35.880
What is something that I can mirror, put that on?

01:06:35.900 --> 01:06:39.722
And I think that right now is the conversation that's closest to home for parents.

01:06:39.942 --> 01:06:40.743
I think that's all that is.

01:06:44.384 --> 01:06:45.105
I'm not a parent.

01:06:45.145 --> 01:06:45.365
Me either.

01:06:46.546 --> 01:06:48.126
I don't know.

01:06:48.767 --> 01:06:51.468
But I think that's something that's,

01:06:52.214 --> 01:06:56.006
no matter what side you're on, that you really need to.

01:06:56.829 --> 01:06:59.177
Even if things make you uncomfortable, as you said.

01:07:04.060 --> 01:07:05.341
No one's attacking you.

01:07:06.041 --> 01:07:06.862
No one's attacking you.

01:07:07.522 --> 01:07:16.147
You know, students, if you are feeling that, you know, if your parents ask you what you're reading and you know they're not going to like something, talk it through them.

01:07:17.348 --> 01:07:19.890
Point to things that you did like, things that you didn't like.

01:07:19.970 --> 01:07:22.972
If you say, like, I completely disagreed with that entire book, move on.

01:07:23.172 --> 01:07:25.833
That's 100% okay.

01:07:26.594 --> 01:07:28.915
I've read books and I'm like, eh, the argument didn't sell me.

01:07:29.175 --> 01:07:29.596
That's okay.

01:07:31.517 --> 01:07:32.978
It can really be as simple as that.

01:07:32.998 --> 01:07:33.518
Mm-hmm.

01:07:34.178 --> 01:07:34.999
It really can be.

01:07:35.239 --> 01:07:39.963
It doesn't have to be, I have to email the person who wrote this, demand they lose their job.

01:07:40.023 --> 01:07:41.664
Like, no, it's not that deep.

01:07:42.045 --> 01:07:42.945
It's really not.

01:07:42.965 --> 01:07:51.593
I think also that people are equating what professors are teaching with what they personally believe.

01:07:51.653 --> 01:07:52.173
Yes.

01:07:52.193 --> 01:07:53.374
Those two things aren't the same.

01:07:53.434 --> 01:07:53.895
No.

01:07:53.915 --> 01:07:53.975
No.

01:07:55.130 --> 01:08:04.134
Like, it kind of, it frustrates me that this actually became the word and the language the university implemented when doing the syllabus reviews.

01:08:04.234 --> 01:08:10.917
But I, on the permanent record, I said, like, educating someone is not advocating.

01:08:12.258 --> 01:08:17.400
So then I kind of bit my tongue when that became the slogan of saying, are you advocating for these ideologies?

01:08:19.426 --> 01:08:19.967
That's so vague.

01:08:20.227 --> 01:08:21.308
That's so vague.

01:08:21.328 --> 01:08:22.549
And they did that on purpose.

01:08:22.609 --> 01:08:27.652
It's easier to just brush everything under a rug and throw it away and light it on fire.

01:08:28.393 --> 01:08:29.614
It's 100% easier.

01:08:30.515 --> 01:08:32.096
How do you know if it's advocating?

